{ netasync driver: builds examples/netasync, runs its echo server with
 * --requests 4, drives four connections through it, verifies the echoes
 * and the clean stop.
 * On Windows the server takes a connection from another process and stops
 * serving (as examples-httpasyncserver.test): known, not yet understood.
 * XFAIL: system-windows
 * RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cp -R %S/../../examples/netasync %t/
 * RUN: rm -rf %t/netasync/bin
 * RUN: cd %t/netasync && %p3-project 2>&1 | count 0
 * RUN: python3 %S/Inputs/netasync-check.py %t/netasync/bin/netasync_demo | FileCheck %s
 * CHECK:      listening: ok
 * CHECK-NEXT: echo 1: one
 * CHECK-NEXT: echo 2: second line
 * CHECK-NEXT: echo 3: third
 * CHECK-NEXT: echo 4: the fourth!
 * CHECK-NEXT: server stopped: ok
  }
